  ready  yeah yeah guy just walked in the door  today and he's got to play tonight  that's on you  you don't have enough guys on the  practice squad to fill in for the guys  who are gone  that's not our problem we are getting  these games in because i think as you've  said before if they would bump it  a couple of days to accommodate the  chiefs and give them a chance to get  fischer and schwartz ready to go there's  no guarantee it's going to be any better  because of the incubation period because  of that doughnut hole in the  sample collection and sample result  you've got to kick the ball when it's on  the tee because you never know when that  virus known as lucy is going to snatch  it away from you and screw  things up so sunday night game on  too bad if you're down your entire  offensive line and patrick mahomes the  most important player  in the league is left to fend for  himself we're getting this game in  mike uh you know a lot of people are  going to look at that and say this is  idiotic  uh it's it's it's a huge mistake  you know there's a reason why you've  made it possible to have a week 18  use it and i think my attitude is look  it's very early in the week you just  don't know  if he loses if they lost their entire  offensive line including backup players  i think then you're going to have to  really ask yourself the question  should they play this game and my answer  would be no absolutely they shouldn't  but a lot of people have asked in recent  weeks  why not just use this why not push it  back and again i know we've talked about  this but  i think it's really important to realize  that you know  the nfl in the middle of march  with free agency three or four days away  basically when the pandemic really hit  the united states  the nfl said hey full speed ahead we're  going ahead with free agency  and the reason why because there was no  guarantee it wasn't going to get any  better  and it didn't get any better exact same  thing happened with the draft did it get  any better no  not for a couple of months after that  and so  i think they're going to do the exact  same thing here  i think the one place and it's only the  one place  where i wouldn't be surprised if there  was some time taken  is the super bowl because once you get  down to one  final game uh if there is a significant  outbreak on one side or the other  i think they might say okay we're  putting these two teams in a bubble  uh in two separate bubbles and we're  gonna do that and then we'll play the  game in two weeks  but before that even if there is a  bubble in the playoffs mike  i doubt sincerely that unless there is a  real widespread outbreak  that they're going to be postponing many  games and the reality at this point  peter and you had a quote from an  unnamed league official in football  morning in america  today there's a sense of beat the clock  when it comes to the pandemic the  numbers are going up dramatically  in all the communities where the nfl has  teams and everywhere else  in the country get the games in  get the games in that's the attitude  they don't want to postpone anything  because we don't know that there even  will be a week 18 or a week 17. it could  be that they ultimately have to pull the  plug after x number of games  so get every game in before we get to  the point where  the house of cards potentially would  collapse on the nfl so i think that's a  big part of it too  there's an urgency to get every game  played regardless of any strategic  realities that could impact one team or  the other  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights  from nbc sports
 

